          %title FrechetUrysohn spaces
          %h1#frecheturysohn_spaces Frechet–Urysohn spaces
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_countability_properties"} Related countability properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#implications"} Implications
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A Frechet–Urysohn (or Frechet–Uryson) space is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closure
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            may be described using only
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Recall that, given any subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of
            %em any
            topological space, a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            belongs to the closure of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is a limit point of at least one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
            whose elements belong to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            A topological space is
            %strong Frechet–Uryson
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong Frechet–Urysohn
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of the closure of any given subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a limit point of at least one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
            whose elements belong to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
