                  %use{:x => "186.784261", "xlink:href" => "#454609461-glyph0-12", :y => "175.967"}
                  %use{:x => "190.326254", "xlink:href" => "#454609461-glyph0-3", :y => "175.967"}
            %p
              Axioms:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              (AC),
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+choice"} countable choice
              (CC).
            %h3#properties Properties
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+space"}> second-countable
                  \: there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+base"} base
                  of the topology.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrisable+topological+space"}> metrisable
                  \: the topology is induced by a metric.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  \-locally discrete base: the topology of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is generated by a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countably+locally+discrete+set+of+subsets"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                    \-locally discrete
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+base"} base
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  \-locally finite base: the topology of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is generated by a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countably+locally+finite+set+of+subsets"} countably locally finite
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+base"} base
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+space"}> separable
                  \: there is a countable
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subspace"} dense
                  subset.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lindel%C3%B6f+topological+space"}> Lindelöf
                  \: every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                  has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+cover"} countable
                  sub-cover.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Lindel%C3%B6f+topological+space"}> weakly Lindelöf
                  \: every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                  has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable
                  subcollection the union of which is dense.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metacompact+space"}> metacompact
                  \: every open cover has a point-finite open refinement.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+chain+condition"}> countable chain condition
                  \: A family of pairwise disjoint open subsets is at most countable.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-countable+space"}> first-countable
                  \: every point has a countable
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood+base"} neighborhood base
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frechet-Uryson+space"}> Frechet-Uryson space
                  \: the closure of a set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  consists precisely of all limit points of sequences in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+topological+space"}> sequential topological space
                  \: a set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is closed if it contains all limit points of sequences in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countably+tight+space"}> countably tight
                  \: for each subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  and each point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mover
                          %mi A
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in \overline A
                  there is a countable subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\subseteq A
                  such that
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mover
                            %mi D
                            %mo ¯
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in \overline D
            %h3#implications Implications
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers+of+metric+spaces+have+open+countably+locally+discrete+refinements"}
                    a metric space has a
                    = succeed "-locally" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nagata-Smirnov+metrization+theorem"} Nagata-Smirnov metrization theorem
              %li
                %p
                  a second-countable space has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countably+locally+finite+set+of+subsets"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                    \-locally finite
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+base"} base
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  second-countable spaces are separable: use the axiom of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+choice"} countable choice
                  to choose a point in each set of a countable cover.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+spaces+are+Lindel%C3%B6f"}> second-countable spaces are Lindelöf
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Lindel%C3%B6f+spaces+with+countably+locally+finite+base+are+second+countable"}> weakly Lindelöf spaces with countably locally finite base are second countable
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+metacompact+spaces+are+Lindel%C3%B6f"}> separable metacompact spaces are Lindelöf
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  separable spaces satisfy the countable chain condition: given a dense set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  and a family
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi α
                          %mo :
                          %mi α
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_\alpha : \alpha \in A\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi α
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \cap \bigcup_{\alpha \in A} U_\alpha \to A
                  assigning
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                  to the unique
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in A
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in U_\alpha
                  is surjective.
              %li
                %p
                  separable spaces are weakly Lindelöf: given a countable dense subset and an open cover
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} choose
                  for each point of the subset an open from the cover.
              %li
                %p Lindelöf spaces are trivially also weakly Lindelöf.
              %li
                %p
                  a space with a
                  = succeed "-locally" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  = succeed "-locally" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %li
                %p a first-countable space is obviously Fréchet-Urysohn.
              %li
                %p a Fréchet-Uryson space is obviously sequential.
              %li
                %p a sequential space is obviously countably tight.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+spaces+satisfying+the+countable+chain+condition+are+Lindel%C3%B6f"}> paracompact spaces satisfying the countable chain condition are Lindelöf
                  \.
